ML Microservice Extracted
To bypass Vercel's strict 128MB serverless function limit, the heavy Machine Learning and Computer Vision models have been successfully extracted into a standalone FastAPI microservice!

This microservice acts as an inference engine that the core app communicates with securely over HTTP.

What was moved to ml_service/:
YOLO ROI Extraction (yolo_roi.py): Runs ONNX-based object detection (yolov8n.onnx and card.onnx) for isolating document zones (Face, MRZ, MRZ Zone).
Aadhaar Field Detection (aadhaar_fields.onnx): Extracts Aadhaar specific fields.
Face Matching (face_match.py): Validates the extracted document portrait against the live selfie using ArcFace/FaceNet embeddings.
AI Generation Detection (main.py -> detect_image): Runs the Vision Transformer (ViT-Base) ONNX model to distinguish between authentic photographs and AI-generated/manipulated imagery.
Microservice Architecture:
Framework: FastAPI
Model runtime: onnxruntime (CPU execution provider)
HTTP Client: Handled inside the core app via httpx
🚀 How to deploy the Microservice for FREE
You requested a free hosting solution for this microservice. I highly recommend Render or Hugging Face Spaces, both of which offer generous free tiers with Docker support.

Using Render (Recommended):

Push this repository to GitHub.
Sign up at render.com and create a new Web Service.
Connect your repository.
Set the "Root Directory" to ml_service.
Render will automatically detect the Dockerfile and build/deploy it for free!
Copy the resulting URL (e.g., https://your-ml-service.onrender.com).
Using Hugging Face Spaces:

Create a new Space at huggingface.co/spaces.
Select Docker as the Space SDK.
Upload the contents of the ml_service/ folder to the space.
It will automatically build and expose the FastAPI endpoints.
Connecting the Vercel App
Once your microservice is deployed and you have its URL, you need to tell your Vercel app where to send ML requests. Go to your Vercel Project Dashboard -> Settings -> Environment Variables and add:

Key: ML_SERVICE_URL
Value: https://your-ml-service-url.com (from Render or HF Spaces)
Redeploy your Vercel app, and it will automatically route all heavy ML inference to your new free-tier microservice, completely bypassing the 128MB bundle limit!

